[4] Readout
  The one-swap finite check supports the boundary-support lemma:
  through add<=160, AP and GW 12->24 are the only boundary-only rows,
  and the first open row is near 12->36 with strict Haar mass 1/1260.
  The two-swap add<=40 check tests the S138 neighborhood for additional
  boundary-only packets; any nonzero count above should be treated as a
  new exact boundary-front obligation, not as Haar-positive evidence.
  HBT*/Haar-Baire Wave should therefore propagate open fronts by measure,
  and route zero-interior boundary fronts to C27/unital/state-lift labels.
